-- title:
--   Conditioning commutes with the normalized selected-state sum
-- statement:
--   Let $n\in\mathbb N$, $E=\{0,\ldots,n-1\}$, and $\widehat E=E\times\{0,1\}$. A partial assignment $\sigma:E\to\{*,0,1\}$ has assigned set $A_\sigma=\{i:\sigma_i\ne *\}$ and selected-label set $C_\sigma=\{(i,\sigma_i):i\in A_\sigma\}$. A paired state respects $\sigma$ when it includes the selected label and excludes its mate at every assigned pair. Let $M_1,M_2$ be matroids on the ambient set $E$, let $q\in\mathbb Q$, and form the paired matroid $N=M_1\oplus M_2^*$, with the first component on labels $(i,0)$ and the second on $(i,1)$. Its homogeneous rank-weight polynomial is $$T(z,y)=\sum_{B\subseteq\widehat E}\bigl(q^{r_N(B)}\bigr)^{-1}z^{2n-|B|}\prod_{e\in B}y_e,$$ where $r_N$ is finite matroid rank and an inverse of zero is interpreted as zero. Put $$D_\sigma=\left(\prod_{e\in C_\sigma}\partial_{y_e}\right)\partial_z^n T,\qquad P_\sigma=\frac{q^n}{n!}\,\Phi_\sigma(D_\sigma),$$ where $\Phi_\sigma$ sets $z$ and both labels of assigned pairs to zero and replaces both labels of each unassigned pair $i$ by $x_i$. For a polynomial $g$ in paired-label variables, define $\mathcal C_\sigma(g)$ by differentiating once at each label in $C_\sigma$, setting both labels of every assigned pair to zero, and identifying the remaining label pair $i$ with $x_i$. Then $$P_\sigma=\mathcal C_\sigma\left(\sum_{\substack{B\subseteq\widehat E\\|B|=n}}q^n\bigl(q^{r_N(B)}\bigr)^{-1}\prod_{e\in B}y_e\right).$$ This expresses the conditioned polynomial as a finite sum of selected-state monomials before occupancy classification.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/meelgroup/counting-matroid/blob/dd16a4628fdb095c58fe0f3dfd8e353c6e97443c/CountingMatroid/Analysis/ConditionalSelectedStateSum.lean#L33-L73

